<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Masmak Fort</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Al Masmak</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Masmak Fort is a clay and mud-brick fortress in the old centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a>, Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>, built in the second half of the 19th century. In January 1902 the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud</a> and a small band of followers captured it from the Rashidi governor, a raid that began the creation of modern Saudi Arabia. It is now a museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/masmak-fort.jpg" alt="Masmak Fort" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francisco Anzola · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Masmak_Fort_(12753717253).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
